	abstract = {As digital technologies continue to advance, cybersecurity has emerged as a complex, multidisciplinary concern spanning domains such as healthcare, finance, IoT, blockchain, AI, and national security. This paper conducts a comprehensive review of more than 150 peer-reviewed studies from 2017 to 2023 to identify key threats, challenges, and strategic responses. Findings reveal alarming trends, including ransomware causing annual global losses above $20 billion and AI-powered attacks bypassing nearly all conventional security systems. Critical infrastructure remains highly exposed to sophisticated, statesponsored cyber threats. Sector-specific approaches are discussed, including zero-trust frameworks in healthcare IoT, blockchain integration for fraud prevention in financial systems, and post-quantum encryption methods for national defense. The paper advocates for stronger cross-sector collaboration, investment in cybersecurity talent, and the creation of unified global standards. It concludes by presenting a future-ready framework to tackle evolving risks, such as those from quantum computing and 5G-enabled cyberattacks, ensuring a more secure and resilient digital environment. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
