	abstract = {The proliferation of Internet of Things (IoT) in smart agriculture generates vast datasets, offering significant benefits but also raising critical privacy concerns. Traditional anonymization methods often prove insufficient against advanced analysis and emerging quantum computing threats, while centralized data management introduces vulnerabilities. This research proposes a novel framework that integrates quantum-resistant blockchain technology (BCT) with advanced data anonymization techniques to ensure privacy preservation in agricultural IoT ecosystems. The proposed approach leverages the decentralized and immutable nature of Blockchain for secure data management and access control, combined with quantum-resistant anonymization methods to protect sensitive agricultural data against both classical and future quantum attacks. This research will explore the design, implementation and evaluation of such a framework, analyzing its performance in terms of privacy guarantees, data utility, computational efficiency, and scalability through simulations and potential real-world case studies. The findings will contribute to the development of secure and privacy-preserving solutions for the responsible adoption of IoT in smart agriculture, addressing the specific needs of various stakeholders in the agricultural value chain. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
