	abstract = {This research proposes a foundational architecture for enabling quantum-safe encryption and blockchain to securely manage legal documents in the cloud. Our protocol offers a pathway to mitigate the existential threat posed by quantum-based attacks to the encryption layers we currently utilize while ensuring its adoption of blockchain technology's transparent and immutable characteristics for legal purposes [1]. Through a thorough examination of three broad families of post-quantum algorithms, i.e., 'lattice-based', 'hash-based', and 'code-based', this study ultimately demonstrates how CRYSTAL-Kyber for encryption and CRYSTAL-Dilithium can support permissioned blockchain networks [2] to ensure the confidentiality of sensitive legal documents. We propose a 3-layer protocol architecture with GDPR-compliant data management architecture with role-based access controls and a multi-stage compliance verification process for legal technology systems. Our legal-tech sustainability checks the erasure algorithm outputs, achieving a 98.6% GDPR erasure success rate, implementing dual key encryption, and being a lawful technology deployment that is geofenced to IPFS. Likewise, our performance evaluation protocol confirmed an operational total time of 42 TPS throughput and 1.84s finality latency while maintaining NIST Level 5 security. Our competition testing still showed (2897) Γ— times faster speed (compared to RSA-2048) while providing quantum-safe encryption while using a minimal key size (1.5 KB) as part of a lawful technology deployment. Our research protocol also improved authentication velocities by 23% and verified 100% compliance on the confirmatory compliance check for cross-border claims.  Β© 2025 IEEE.},
