thms. All of these optimizations give substantial improvements for small s and a reasonable choice of r. Finally, we formalize the notion of linear equivalence of block ciphers and prove the optimality of some of our results. Comprehensive benchmarking of our optimizations in various LOWMC applications (such as PICNIC) reveals improvements by factors that typically range between 2x and 40x in runtime and memory consumption. Β© International Association for Cryptologic Research 2019.},
